"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Liv","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"3e3e8e6d-7e51-4773-9f11-86146f6ab3a2","name":"Bjerre, Liv","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","name":"Papazu, Irina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01064142","09057633"],"issn_org":["01064142"],"newspaper":"Weekendavisen","publisher":"Berlingske Media AS","publisher_org":"Berlingske Media A/S","status":"p","title":"Weekendavisen"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8746c102-ee8c-4f42-b180-d179cd861283","ku-b26dbca1-3c00-4e0f-bd65-93f97d8f9442"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kontroverser, hvor der er konsensus","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.16-716027","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, countries like France, UK, Germany, and Denmark have all carried out climate citizens’ assemblies where a group of representatively selected citizens come together to discuss issues around climate politics and provide policy recommendations to decision-makers. The hope is that these deliberative-democratic innovations can circumvent the flaws of representational politics and help break the existing gridlock around climate politics. In this article, relying on the case of the Danish climate citizens’ assembly that began its work in 2020, we argue that to truly realize the democratic potentials of climate citizens’ assemblies, there is a need to think about how citizens’ assemblies might come to multiply and proliferate in political spaces away from, or at least in addition to, those in and around the state, so they can become local drivers of democratic action and community empowerment. The argument is not that citizens’ assemblies should give up on affecting the state and parliamentary politics altogether, but that we must be careful not to put too much faith in state institutions, and also look for spaces outside the state where the conditions for transformative change and democratic capacity-building currently appear more fecund. Drawing together these arguments, we offer what we call a more radical vision of the democratic potentials of climate citizens’ assemblies, and provide some guidelines for what that would look like in practice.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ejsing, Mads","Veng, Adam","Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S02-097.91-673004"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Citizens assemblies","Climate governance","Deliberative democracy","Democratic innovation","Faculty of Social Sciences","Mini publics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"green politics beyond the state radicalizing the democratic potentials of climate citizens assemblies","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10584-023-03550-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.91-673004","identifier":[{"id":"37273888","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85160797485","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10227389","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["itu-bfff5bed-3cd1-4809-a72d-3e99d0361818","ku-a6d13a23-e91d-4eef-aee0-ea33f1e20fc0"],"keyword":["Citizens' assemblies","Climate governance","Deliberative democracy","Democratic innovation","Faculty of Social Sciences","Mini-publics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0FBE6C05CDB7CB6CF9E2FE8147173B97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347706252/s10584_023_03550_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10584-023-03550-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/99174930/s10584_023_03550_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Political Theory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"ejsingpau","last":"Ejsing","locid":"21259a0e-430d-4479-b828-7aef6b117850","name":"Ejsing, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-6498-5318","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Adam","key":"vengpau","last":"Veng","name":"Veng, Adam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37273888"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10584-023-03550-z","issn":["01650009","15731480"],"issn_org":["15731480"],"issue":"73","journal":"Climatic Change","pages":"1-19","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Climatic Change","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160797485"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bfff5bed-3cd1-4809-a72d-3e99d0361818","ku-a6d13a23-e91d-4eef-aee0-ea33f1e20fc0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Green Politics Beyond the State : Radicalizing the Democratic Potentials of Climate Citizens’ Assemblies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.91-673004","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This article is based on digital methods research using the tools Hyphe, Gephi and CorText to map the relations between public Danish actors – from informal civil society groups and NGO’s to business and state actors - and their “matters of concern” (cf. Latour 2004) in the heated political situation around the development of green transition policies following the enactment of the Climate Act in 2019. The Act was, according to the newly elected social democratic government, the “most ambitious Climate Act in the world”. It included such political innovations as the Citizens’ Assembly on Climate Change, a group of 99 randomly selected citizens mandated to give recommendations to parliament, and a series of Climate Partnerships, business and industry collaborations tasked with developing recommendations and frameworks for the business community’s engagement in the green transition. The Climate Act was passed after massive popular pressure from the civic climate movement leading up to the election. Despite these efforts and the apparent political will to engage with multiple voices and interests, our network mapping shows that the business community, with an emphasis on “innovative and technological solutions”, were soon to become dominant in the network and align themselves more closely with the political system than the civil society actors were able to with their repeated calls for more radical and political action on climate change.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Veng, Adam","Papazu, Irina","Ejsing, Mads"],"cuid":["S02-090.50-686170"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Climate change","Controversy Mapping","Digital Methods","Green transition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"is denmark a green entrepreneurial state mapping danish climate politics between civic mobilization and business cooptation","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v15i2.139817","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.50-686170","ids":["itu-1517cac9-4bd5-44ee-b555-9392eec95f7c","ku-5f41a0d0-d729-4c9f-bf87-dd29dda2ff4c"],"keyword":["Climate Change","Controversy Mapping","Digital Methods","Green Transition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-56104F3875CBE37088838DCBA442040A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/encounters/article/view/139817/183845","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/encounters/article/download/139817/183845/303522","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v15i2.139817","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/365874226/15_2_Veng_et_al_green_entrepreneurial_2023.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Adam","key":"vengpau","last":"Veng","locid":"737721f0-dcbb-48c4-81bf-e8e5e07d3248","name":"Veng, Adam","orcid":"0000-0001-5162-791X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"ejsingpau","last":"Ejsing","locid":"21259a0e-430d-4479-b828-7aef6b117850","name":"Ejsing, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-6498-5318","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/stse.v15i2.139817","issn":["19044372"],"issue":"2","journal":"STS Encounters","status":"p","title":"STS Encounters","title_org":"STS Encounters - DASTS working paper series","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1517cac9-4bd5-44ee-b555-9392eec95f7c","ku-5f41a0d0-d729-4c9f-bf87-dd29dda2ff4c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Is Denmark a green entrepreneurial state? : Mapping Danish climate politics between civic mobilization and business cooptation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.50-686170","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
