{"abstract":"Entrepreneurial resource construction through bricolage is an underappreciated element in a growing body of entrepreneurship and organization studies examining bricolage as an organizational strategy under conditions of resource scarcity. Drawing on in-depth ethnographic data, this study of the Danish island Samsø’s successful transition to renewable energy argues for a richer understanding and a more positive appraisal of entrepreneurial bricolage as a multifaceted strategy for change on the community level. By demonstrating the constructed nature of the resource environments identified on Samsø, the article argues that bricolage, rather than revolving around the combination of already available resources to create new entrepreneurial ventures, is a process involving the construction of resources to achieve change. An in-depth understanding of this process of resource construction is especially relevant in the context of local sustainable energy transitions, as bricolage, in this context, can enable the community to work towards a shared goal without accepting the constraints of the resource-scarce local environment.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384055"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bricolage","Entrepreneurship","Ethnography","renewable energy transitions","resource construction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entrepreneurial resource construction through collective bricolage on denmark s renewable energy island an ethnographic study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08985626.2021.1964613","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384055","identifier":[{"id":"85112038218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-be1e2f8d-a0bd-4df4-a30d-d36f58d10d99"],"keyword":["Bricolage","entrepreneurship","ethnography","renewable energy transitions","resource construction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-34E47941873DB8702E4192E5075D95E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08985626.2021.1964613","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/08985626.2021.1964613?casa_token=Uu238h6aXnYAAAAA:NYYUO14FWbfB7HzjXCYPVfLXtoOePKZaQ5G5rfZZY3ge2PfVo1h86KvAJb-kpSW6NWSUCafkeGY2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08985626.2021.1964613","issn":["08985626","14645114"],"issn_org":["08985626"],"journal":"Entrepreneurship & Regional Development","pages":"1-26","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Entrepreneurship & Regional Development"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112038218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Pub