"],"title":"Det er tid til at afvikle den danske produktion af fossil energi","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382928","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This case study is based on my methodological reflections during and after conducting ethnographic fieldwork on Samsø, Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island, for my doctoral thesis. Interested in how the citizens of Samsø managed to “renew” their island through the installation of new energy infrastructures and in how the island’s subsequent status as a globally renowned renewable energy transition role model was managed, the fieldwork proved a continually evolving process of knowledge formation. In this case study, I discuss the process of knowledge production through a distinction between “traditional ethnography” and “ethnography as empirical philosophy.” The latter describes my ethnographic journey as characterized by relations of complicity with my research subjects, by difficulties with keeping the different stages of the research project separate (perhaps these distinctions were fragile constructs to begin with), and by the need for alternative evaluative criteria prioritizing surprise and flexibility over a rigorous and systematic research plan. Importantly, these seeming troubles of the research process, in an “empirical philosophy” perspective, become productive moments of knowledge formation where new insights are generated. As a pedagogical tool, the case highlights not only the challenges but also the benefits of working exploratively in such a way that the object of study is not fixated or narrowly defined but rather allowed to emerge and take different shapes in the course of the fieldwork process.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-292559"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ethnography as empirical philosophy studying samsø s renewable energy transition","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-292559","ids":["cbs-b49e08a1-d2e3-4127-bc5c-c6761f4787b3"],"keyword":["Renewable energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-61D4566F1DE59136C0CFBB1B50FC7C57"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-b49e08a1-d2e3-4127-bc5c-c6761f4787b3"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Ethnography as Empirical Philosophy : Studying Samsø’s Renewable Energy Transition","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-292559","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Organization studies have shown limited interest in the part that scaling plays in organizational responses to climate change and sustainability. Moreover, while scales are viewed as central to the diagnosis of the organizational challenges posed by climate change and sustainability, the role of scaling in meeting these challenges has not yet been recognized. By analysing two ethnographic case studies, conducted at Samsø Energy Academy and Farendløse Cider Works, respectively, the authors identify scaling as a core activity of the sustainability organization. The two organizations studied each situate their operations at the heart of the climate change problematic – one in organic farming, the other in renewable energy – and, employing what the authors term ‘the method of scaling’, they impose order on the world in which they operate. The method of scaling helps the organizations relate their actions to the ambiguous concepts of sustainability and climate change. The authors find that the two organizations’ scaling activities occur in three modes: rejection, innovation and conscious adoption of core concepts such as sustainability and climate change. These modes of scaling help organizations turn something as immense as the climate into a small and manageable problem, thus making abstract concepts part of concrete, organizational practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina","Nelund, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-089.66-031501"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Climate change","Ethnographic Case Studies","Organizational Responses","Scaling","Sustainability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scaling as an organizational method ethnographic explorations of two danish sustainability organizations","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045441621","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.66-031501","identifier":[{"id":"85045441621","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-531a3d41-09d4-4007-91c6-de410958565c","itu-9e480ebe-1200-4a35-b5b6-87970ed49985"],"keyword":["Climate Change","Ethnographic Case Studies","Organizational Responses","Scaling","Sustainability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3A7E1ABB79C8736093D31C17DF737E01"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nelundpau","last":"Nelund","locid":"229b4818-b981-4afe-a081-84db5e176c6e","name":"Nelund, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1467-8551.12288","issn":["10453172","14678551"],"issn_org":["10453172"],"issue":"2","journal":"British Journal of Management","pages":"252-265","publisher":"Blackwell Publishing","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Management","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045441621"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-531a3d41-09d4-4007-91c6-de410958565c","itu-9e480ebe-1200-4a35-b5b6-87970ed49985"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scaling as an Organizational Method : Ethnographic Explorations of Two Danish Sustainability Organizations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.66-031501","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Through a joint community effort Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island Samsø became self-sufficient with renewable energy over a period of 10 years from 1997 to 2007. Today, the story about Samsø’s successful energy transition has become a global export and a widely known model of community building, public participation and shared ownership in renewable energy technologies and transition processes. What has allowed the Samsø narrative to travel so widely has been the effective ‘transition story’ created about the islanders’ efforts. This transition story, however, has become fixed with the years and has assumed an ideal-typical character. Meanwhile, the challenges and costs inherent in the complicated socio-material process of transition are underestimated and largely forgotten. While such transition stories are indeed inspiring, the ideal-typical narrative may stand in the way of the development of further local energy transitions, as challenging elements of the process are downplayed to strengthen the narrative power of the story. Ethnographic stories about Samsø complicate the island’s transition narrative and add nuance to the Samsø story, highlighting its discrepancies and problematizing the effects of such well-crafted transition narratives. This tendency toward the ‘storification’ of transition processes is not restricted to Samsø; it is employed as a tactics by environmental organizations operating globally.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-277117"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ethnography","Local energy transitions","Renewable energy","Transition stories"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"storifying samsøs renewable energy transition","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/57305604/irina_papazu_storifying_sams_s_renewable_energy_transition_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-277117","identifier":[{"id":"85034229855","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-12949b64-1256-460f-9636-50d01ff3a0ac"],"keyword":["Ethnography","Local energy transitions","Renewable energy","Transition stories"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A4AAB193703AD781F6FCC3206A8D236"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/57305604/irina_papazu_storifying_sams_s_renewable_energy_transition_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09505431.2017.1398224","issn":["09505431","14701189"],"issn_org":["09505431"],"issue":"2","journal":"Science as Culture","pages":"198-220","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Science as Culture","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034229855"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-12949b64-1256-460f-9636-50d01ff3a0ac"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Storifying Samsøs Renewable Energy Transition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-277117","year":"2018","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The Danish island Samsø is world-famous as Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island. 21 wind turbines supply the island’s electricity. Today, public hostility toward a projected nearshore wind farm off the island’s preserved northern coast is growing. This paper takes its main theoretical cue from Gomartand Hajer’s (2003) call to open up political questions to empirical inquiry and to pay attention to the material settings in which political questions unfold. The paper seeks to make sense of the islanders’ unexpected opposition to a new wind farm, and it does so through a critique of the unexperimental and depoliticizing attitude – found in the empirical case as well as in some academic scholarship – of the NIMBY (Not In My BackYard) logic. Replacing the NIMBY logic of closing down deliberation with an empirical and ‘cosmopolitical’ (Stengers, 2005) approach to open up the space of politics to close investigation, the paper focuses on the empirical settings which give the controversy its specifi c shape and asks how the projected wind farm is interrogated, negotiated and recast as it travels through the socio-material politics of the wind controversy.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-287971"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Controversy studies","NIMBY","Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nearshore wind resistance on denmark s renewable energy island not another nimby story","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23987/sts.60523","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-287971","identifier":[{"id":"85017502576","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-8401f79c-4191-4863-8ac1-f854b4a3debd"],"keyword":["Controversy studies","NIMBY","Renewable energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-14E36A9961A3B4C851BED15D094E383F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://sciencetechnologystudies.journal.fi/article/view/60523/22488","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23987/sts.60523","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23987/sts.60523","issn":["22434690"],"issue":"1","journal":"Science & Technology Studies","pages":"4-24","publisher":"Finnish Society for Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"Science & Technology Studies","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017502576"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-8401f79c-4191-4863-8ac1-f854b4a3debd"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Nearshore Wind Resistance on Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island : Not Another NIMBY Story","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-287971","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Anmeldelser af: Lasse Folke Henriksen og Christian Waldstrøm (2016): Netværksanalyse - En introduktion. Samfundslitteratur. 112 sider. Og Andreas Birkbak og Anders Kristian Munk (2017): Digitale Metoder. Hans Reitzels Forlag. 200 sider.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-288537"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"netværksanalyse med og uden internettet","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djb","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/index.php/politik/article/viewFile/81579/138420","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-288537","ids":["cbs-8a7d406e-17ec-478b-a250-4b8d61465f50"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F6A3F3AC48DA50D17724A4FAB0AD354"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/index.php/politik/article/viewFile/81579/138420","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16040058","24460893"],"issn_org":["16040058"],"issue":"2","journal":"Politik","pages":"127-131","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p","title":"Politik","volume":"20"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-8a7d406e-17ec-478b-a250-4b8d61465f50"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Netværksanalyse : Med og uden internettet","type":"Journal Book Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-288537","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"How are we to understand politics if antagonism (Mouffe 2005) and disagreement (Rancière 1998) have no parts to play? Through the case of Samsø, Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island since 1999, I seek to expand our theoretical understanding of politics, usually conceptualized as a conflictridden process, an “unpleasant” (Brown 2015) battle between diverging interests. I investigate and attempt to turn this understanding of politics around by engaging the case of Samsø, where I conducted ethnographic fieldwork in 2013 and 14. The rural island community of Samsø managed to become self-sufficient with renewable energy over a ten-year period, notably without sparking much controversy or disagreement among the islanders. The results of the project were not simply wind turbines, district heating plants and solar systems but also new jobs, a heightened level of activity on the island and hope for the future, and, I argue, through the process and accomplishment of the Renewable Energy Island project, a strengthened sense of community and confidence among the islanders. By viewing the island as a climate laboratory invested in creating and revitalizing communities not only locally but nationally, regionally and globally, I ask: if indeed such a process of renewal must be understood as a political process and the island’s energy transition as an inherently political event, what can Samsø teach us about the workings of politics and local democracy as enacted in practice? This is politics not as election result or ideological struggle over values, ideals and the distribution of goods, but as the down-to-earth but significant activity of creating something new together.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-280044"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-02","place":"Gothenburg, se","start":"2017-05-31","title":"Third Nordic Science and Technology Studies (STS) Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"renewing samsø re conceptualizing politics as a process of community renewal","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://socav.gu.se/digitalAssets/1642/1642685_all-abstracts-170530.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-280044","ids":["cbs-31285952-83ff-4657-86b2-d331535b4aef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-66F569336CD58C4C3F2C37BA60423076"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://socav.gu.se/digitalAssets/1642/1642685_all-abstracts-170530.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"66","place":"Gothenburg","publisher":"Göteborg Universitet","status":"p","subtitle":"Third Nordic Science and Technology Conference","title":"Abstracts"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-31285952-83ff-4657-86b2-d331535b4aef"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Renewing Samsø : Re-conceptualizing Politics as a Process of Community Renewal","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-280044","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Parliaments could seem to be highly issue-agnostic places. All sorts of problems move in and out. But issues make cuts. Some parliamentarians become attached to specific issues. What if the parliament was approached not as a representation device for the national population, but as an assembly of multiple and constantly transforming issue-oriented publics? What kinds of issues come to the fore, how long does this last, and who associate themselves with them? The aim of the Twitter-thing is to trace the cuts issues make in a parliament. Each time a parliamentarian use a hashtag in a tweet, a link is created between that hashtag and the parliamentarian. The tool then generates a network visualization showing how parliamentarians group around topics and issues. The resulting ‘issue publics’ – or things in the sense of a collective aroused by an issue – are also ‘data publics’ because they are not necessarily aware of themselves as publics. At the same time, it is possible to self-select membership of these publics by using a specific hashtag. This raises the question of what feedback loops are at work between visualizations and those being visualized. How might a tool like the Twitter-thing change (parliamentary) politics? More generally, the tool prompts us to think about the fate of issues in institutionalized democracy. The Twitter-thing invites users to explore these questions by making the network available in an interactive format that makes it possible to zoom, search for particular politicians, parties or hashtags, narrow down the network, and follow it over time.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Birkbak, Andreas","Bornakke, Tobias","Papazu, Irina Maria Clara Hansen"],"cuid":["S02-082.21-010332"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-02","place":"Lancaster, gb","start":"2017-03-31","title":"Data Publics","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the twitter thing exhibition retooling the parliament into issue publics","src":["aau","cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://twitterting.cadm.dk/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.21-010332","ids":["aau-d86afbae-c149-4693-9033-aa0683a08971","cbs-35c3d27c-06c7-48b7-adfd-10cfa2d734de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-54569A1404C41263D4CD92F70BF86EB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://twitterting.cadm.dk/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, The Techno-Anthropology Research Group (Learning)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Sociologisk Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"birkbakpau","last":"Birkbak","locid":"269bb408-d628-47f8-8539-d0c4b97a9aad","name":"Birkbak, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-9283-1677","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"bornakkepau","last":"Bornakke","name":"Bornakke, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina Maria Clara Hansen","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","name_org":"Papazu, Irina Maria Clara Hansen","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d86afbae-c149-4693-9033-aa0683a08971","cbs-35c3d27c-06c7-48b7-adfd-10cfa2d734de"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Twitter-things : Retooling the Parliament into Issue-oriented Data Publics","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.21-010332","year":"2017","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Purpose – The purpose of this paper is to analyse the process of social and technical change that took place between 1997 and 2007 through which Samsø, a rural island of 4,000 inhabitants, became Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island (REI). Design/methodology/approach – Building on ethnographic fieldwork conducted on Samsø in 2013 and 2014, the paper takes as its starting point a citizens’ meeting in which a new renewable energy project is proposed by a municipal coordinator. This meeting, in which the municipal coordinator exhibits a “change management” attitude, fails to win the citizens’ support and becomes an entry point into an investigation of how the REI project developers managed to get the island community to actively support the project. A gateway to the past, the meeting allows the author to ethnographically describe the unobserved events of 1997-2007. Findings – The argument is that the REI project developers practised management through hope or “hope management”, in contrast to “change management”, creating a project that succeeded in accomplishing its goals of changing the island due to its openness, its rootedness in the island community’s past, and the project developers’ ability to speak to a down-to-earth variety of hope. Originality/value – The paper makes use of an ethnographic study of the present to investigate an unobserved past in which a REI was built. Taking up the “hope debate” in anthropology and Science and Technology Studies (Stengers, 2002; Miyazaki, 2004; Jensen, 2014), the paper contributes with an empirical analysis of the role of hope in the management of change processes.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-277599"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"management through hope an ethnography of denmark s renewable energy island","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-277599","identifier":[{"id":"84981505095","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-176080e5-b4f5-49c4-ba5d-4fb30f9ea629"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E9629D57BEAC02E43DBACA6F1F75F75"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/joe-11-2015-0025","issn":["20466749"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Organizational Ethnography","pages":"184-200","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing","status":"p","title":"Journal of Organizational Ethnography","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84981505095"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-176080e5-b4f5-49c4-ba5d-4fb30f9ea629"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Management Through Hope : An Ethnography of Denmark’s Renewable Energy Island","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-277599","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Samsø, Denmark's Renewable Energy Island since 1997, is world renowned for being self-sufficient in renewable energy and for having achieved energy self-sufficiency and CO2 neutrality through successful processes of public participation. In this article I seek to show how these processes of public participation so central to the Renewable Energy Island project can be better understood as instances of material participation motivated first and foremost by a concern for the future of the island as a 'liveable' community; a community in which jobs and institutions are not constantly threatening to disappear. By turning to material participation, a concept inspired by Noortje Marres and Jennifer Gabrys, the efforts put into Samsø’s energy transformation by the islanders are given specificity. While much literature on public participation foregrounds public meetings and other spaces for deliberation and debate, material participation locates participation in everyday practice and work. On Samsø, the islanders’ participation was not an add-on to the project, it was an indispensable resource in itself. Building on extensive fieldwork I analyse how the islanders came to invest their time and resources in the Renewable Energy Island project, highlighting how, by materializing energy in concrete, local projects, energy and climate change-related projects can gain community-strengthening potentialities reaching beyond goals of energy self-sufficiency.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-295542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"authoring participation","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/44995915/irina_papazu_authoring_participation_publishers_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-295542","ids":["cbs-d3ccdfcd-b9df-4bb1-9dbf-24aac4a6a656"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-ADA35B382BB1620CED4A2CCBCAB15FCA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/44995915/irina_papazu_authoring_participation_publishers_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nordicsts.org/index.php?journal=njsts&page=article&op=view&path%5B%5D=Papazu&path%5B%5D=pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"9379df03-c67e-4bfd-84c5-7d4332ddc280","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18944647"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordic Journal of Science and Technology Studies","pages":"17-31","publisher":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Science and Technology Studies","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-d3ccdfcd-b9df-4bb1-9dbf-24aac4a6a656"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Authoring Participation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-295542","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This article engages in the discussion that was initially framed by Elizabeth Shove (2010) about the relevance of social practice theory compared to behaviorist theory regarding the question of how citizens may be engaged in more sustainable everyday behaviors or practices. We put both theories to work by analyzing our empirical data from the point of view of each theoretical perspective. Through a discussion of these opposing analyses, the paper concludes that the social practice approach provides a more coherent and grounded perspective on individual climate engagement. Key Words: Climate change—Individual engagement—Social practice theory—Behaviorism.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina","Scheele, Christian Elling"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463904"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"changing individual behaviours or creating green societies advancing from a behaviourist to a social practice theory approach","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://online.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/eco.2014.0060","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-463904","identifier":[{"id":"84933510820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-75d29baa-0647-47a5-88f0-6466256b90ab"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-888A00DF25867FE6922037FA36A8A344"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6a881b01-5f90-46d7-95d7-40fbf3548611","name":"Papazu, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Elling","key":"scheelepau","last":"Scheele","locid":"488392c0-3254-4890-9e43-7bd6380dde2e","name":"Scheele, Christian Elling","orcid":"0000-0002-3009-2984","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/eco.2014.0060","issn":["19429347"],"issue":"2","journal":"Ecopsychology","pages":"104-111","paperid":"7","status":"p","title":"Ecopsychology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84933510820"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-75d29baa-0647-47a5-88f0-6466256b90ab"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Changing individual behaviours or creating green societies? : Advancing from a behaviourist to a social practice theory approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463904","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the preceding chapter, Jens Hoff argued that we are witnessing a qualitative shift in the authorities´apporach to citizen involvement in the area of climate change. The Character of the involvement is changing as more power seems to be delegated to the citizens who are encouraged to get engaged and invest more aspects of their lives in the pursuit of less CO2-intensive lifestyles. This chapter argues that we may need a new theoretical and methodological framework that can take into account the complexity charaterising citizen participation and engagement in the climate change problematic. Through the empirical analysis of a local climate project, ´The Climate Family Project´, in the Danish municipality of Ballerup, it will be illustrated that a turn towards the body of work collectively referred to as Science & Technology Studies (STS) will enlighten our analysis and increase our understanding of the complicated processes at work in strengthening citizen engagement with the climate. Actor-network theory (ANT) and post-ANT will be applied to the analysis of ´The Climate Family Project´, while at the same time attending to the broader research question: What value might STS perspectives add to analyses of citizen participation in the policy area of climate change? ","author_count":3,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525506"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the materialisation of participation in a municipality near you","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-525506","identifier":[{"id":"84949223608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dd169bb5-f237-4ca8-a587-e66f47228c5d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-37EB07C33A9F86A945481D3D95F451DA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6a881b01-5f90-46d7-95d7-40fbf3548611","name":"Papazu, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"hoffpedh","last":"Hoff","name":"Hoff, Jens","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Quentin","key":"gaussetpedh","last":"Gausset","name":"Gausset, Quentin","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781315700298"],"isbn":["9781138901094"],"pages":"54-68","place":"London/New York","publisher":"Routledge","series":"Routledge Advances in Climate Change Research","status":"p","title":"Community governance and citizen driven initiatives in climate change mitigation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949223608"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dd169bb5-f237-4ca8-a587-e66f47228c5d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the materialisation of participation in a municipality near you","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-525506","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482881"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Borgerinddragelse","Det Samfundsvidenskabelige Fakultet","Grøn omstilling"],"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skygger kæmpevindmøllerne for udsynet","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jyllands-posten.dk/aarhus/meninger/breve/ECE6762013/skygger-kaempevindmoellerne-for-udsynet/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-482881","ids":["ku-95babaac-6247-4581-9a01-2e5cf432d37c"],"keyword":["Det Samfundsvidenskabelige Fakultet","borgerinddragelse","grøn omstilling","kystnære vindmøller"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5D98A5A32897714A364DF8839E3C2D22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jyllands-posten.dk/aarhus/meninger/breve/ECE6762013/skygger-kaempevindmoellerne-for-udsynet/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6a881b01-5f90-46d7-95d7-40fbf3548611","name":"Papazu, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01091182"],"newspaper":"Jyllands-Posten","pages":"11","status":"p","title":"Jyllands-Posten","title_org":"Jyllands Posten"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-95babaac-6247-4581-9a01-2e5cf432d37c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Skygger kæmpevindmøllerne for udsynet?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482881","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This article introduces a device-centred approach to the concept of climate engagement through a qualitative analysis of two websites: www.klimabevidst.dk and www.mapmyclimate.dk. While www.klimabevidst.dk represents a down-to-earth take on individual engagement with the climate, providing users with hands-on guides to green home improvements, www.mapmyclimate.dk seeks to increase the user’s awareness of the phenomenon of global climate change by demonstrating how the user’s actions impact the earth’s future. Through conversations with six individuals centred on these green technologies, we investigate how the scaling techniques employed by the websites impact the user’s sense of agency vis-à-vis the climate. The analysis suggests that scales can indeed be changed or redefined in a way conducive to climate engagement.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina","Scheele, Christian Elling"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-546062"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de localising the climate the production of uncertain agencies through climate websites","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.dasts.dk/wp-content/uploads/Papazu-Scheele.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-546062","ids":["ku-ffd40fe2-92b7-486a-a96e-da5fb998d232"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2186AAA1192F7CC84C1BCEA22AB5F4CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.dasts.dk/wp-content/uploads/Papazu-Scheele.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6a881b01-5f90-46d7-95d7-40fbf3548611","name":"Papazu, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Elling","key":"scheelepau","last":"Scheele","locid":"488392c0-3254-4890-9e43-7bd6380dde2e","name":"Scheele, Christian Elling","orcid":"0000-0002-3009-2984","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19044372"],"issue":"1","journal":"STS Encounters","pages":"1-33","status":"p","title":"STS Encounters","title_org":"STS Encounters - DASTS working paper series","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ffd40fe2-92b7-486a-a96e-da5fb998d232"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"(De)-Localising the Climate : The production of uncertain agencies through climate websites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-546062","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
